            <ArticleTitle>[Pain relief].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3750-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain in palliative patients demonstrates impact from many dimensions. This article focuses on pain and typical treatment problems in this respect. A pain analysis is mandatory before initiating pharmacological treatment. However, there are often problems with neuropathic and breakthrough pain. A special issue is the possible toxicity of opioids with acute tolerance and central nervous system sensitisation resulting in increased pain intensity. A key word in the treatment of opioid induced problems is opioid rotation. As pain is very dynamic, close monitoring is recommended.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
